{
  "schema": "ld-s10y-image/figure-spec@2",
  "id": "fig-64",
  "mode": "deterministic",
  "description": "Read the source-plotted function g on its stated bounded domain; retain half-unit cells, solid curve and axis values without adding a query line, a formula or answer annotation.",
  "source": {
    "image": {
      "path": "ssot-resources/soviet10year-textbooks/artifacts/7a/figures/fig-64.png",
      "sha256": "4fc74e8217062f68efcad41958aaf2f1047a99ee0dfdfd7c88c3d84ccdd0d4d8"
    },
    "authoritativeText": [
      {
        "lesson": "alg7-c4-ex",
        "exercise": "939",
        "text": "939. 函数$g$由图象给出（图64），它的定义域是区间$[-2,5]$。利用图象求命题为真的集合（说出回答的理由）：\na) $g(x)=-0.5$；\nb) $g(x)<-0.5$；\nc) $g(x)>-0.5$。"
      }
    ],
    "inventory": [
      {
        "id": "single-source-grid",
        "description": "One shared rectangular lattice with 19 vertical lines and 13 horizontal lines: 18 columns by 12 rows, step 0.5 on both axes, zero phase; x runs -2.5..6.5, y runs -2..4. Grid line gaps around printed axis values and isolated scan breaks are typography/damage, not missing cells. The deliberate dashed domain-endpoint guide at x=-2 is inventoried separately, not classified as damage. Rectification of scanning skew is modern.",
        "objects": [
          "source-half-unit-grid"
        ],
        "assertions": [
          "source-grid-18-by-12"
        ],
        "requires": [
          "gridDimensions"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "source-axes-and-labels",
        "description": "Horizontal x and vertical y cross at the sole printed origin 0 and point in the positive directions. Printed x values: [-2, -1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5]; printed y values: -1, 1, 2, 3. There are no printed half-unit values, curve-name labels, point letters or units. Modern labels are offset to keep clear of strokes; for g, nonnegative x values move above their unchanged tick positions so the descending curve cannot obscure them. The existing sole zero keeps its anchor (0,0.45) and is placed west of the y-axis for clear space. These side changes are modern, not source label-placement facts.",
        "objects": [
          "source-x-axis",
          "source-y-axis",
          "source-x-direction",
          "source-y-direction",
          "source-x-value-minus-2",
